  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "The current best (config_042: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + concat, acc=0.715) uses the strongest encoder pair found so far. The only untested design dimension with this encoder combination is aggregation method. With scgpt, transformer aggregation was slightly worse than avgpool (0.494 vs 0.525), but scvi_n200 produces more structured, denoised latent representations that may benefit from attention-based aggregation in a way the weaker scgpt features did not. Config_018 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) directly tests this hypothesis while keeping the concat fusion that already outperformed weighted (0.715 vs 0.706). This is the highest-information experiment remaining: if transformer aggregation helps, it could push accuracy above 0.715; if not, it confirms avgpool is optimal and frees the final experiment for a cheaper refinement. Expected cost is high (~12–15 GPU hours) due to the transformer aggregation layer over ViT-L features, but the potential accuracy gain and the fact that we still have one experiment of budget remaining make this the best use of experiment 8."
}

